---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ExternalLink from "@/components/ExternalLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About projectcert — mission, approach, and how to contribute."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink">About</h1>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-muted">
      projectcert is an atlas of teacher certification requirements for
      instructing classified English Learner (EL) students across the
      U.S. — every state and the District of Columbia.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Why</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      Under <em>Lau v. Nichols</em> (1974) and subsequent federal
      regulations, students classified as ELs are legally entitled to
      meaningful access to the curriculum. Whether that promise is met
      depends heavily on whether the teacher in front of them has been
      trained to make it real. SEAs determine teacher credentialing.
      Their requirements vary widely. This site catalogs the variation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What's here</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-ink-muted space-y-1">
      <li>An <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/map/">interactive map</a> with five layers.</li>
      <li>Topical reports on <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/credentials/bilingual/">bilingual</a>, <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/credentials/eld/">ELD</a>, and <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/credentials/sei/">SEI</a> credentials.</li>
      <li>A <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/standards/">standards-mention dashboard</a> for whether each SEA's professional teaching standards reference EL students.</li>
      <li>A <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/compare/">side-by-side comparison</a> tool.</li>
      <li>A <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/states/ma/">page for every state</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Source paper</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      Leider, C. M., Colombo, M. W., &amp; Nerlino, E. (2021).
      Decentralization, teacher quality, and the education of English
      learners: Do state education agencies effectively prepare teachers
      of ELs? <em>Education Policy Analysis Archives, 29</em>(100).
      <ExternalLink class="text-accent hover:underline" href="https://doi.org/10.14507/epaa.29.5279">https://doi.org/10.14507/epaa.29.5279</ExternalLink>
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Contributing</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      State data lives as JSON files in the project repo. To propose an
      update — new SEA documents, changed credentialing requirements,
      corrections — file an issue or open a PR with the source URL and
      date.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
